# The frontend needs no environment variables.
#
# Every request goes to this site's own /api, and the proxy in front of it decides
# where that lands: vite.config.js in development, vercel.json once deployed. So there
# is nothing to keep correct here, and a value set on the hosting service is ignored.
#
# VITE_API_URL used to be read, and being read is what broke sign-in twice — a stale
# host baked into the bundle, then a base missing /api. It is ignored now on purpose.
#
# To develop against a different backend, edit the proxy target in vite.config.js
# (currently http://localhost:5000). That file runs on your machine, so the address
# never ends up inside anything you ship.
